---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { PRICE } from "../data/site";

const title = "Terms of Service | PaintingPricing Calculator";
const description = "The terms that apply to using PaintingPricing Calculator's free tools and Pro workspace.";
---

<LegalLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="September 17, 2026"
>
  <section>
    <p>
      These terms apply to your use of PaintingPricing Calculator ("we,"
      "us," "the Site") at paintingpricingcalculator.com, including the
      free tools and the paid Pro workspace. By using the Site, you agree
      to these terms. If you don't agree, don't use the Site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the Site is</h2>
    <p>
      PaintingPricing Calculator is a set of estimating and pricing tools
      for painting contractors: free job-cost, interior, and estimate
      template calculators, plus an optional paid Pro workspace with
      reusable rates, multi-surface projects, and profitability tracking.
      It's a calculation aid, not professional, financial, legal, or
      business advice — see the <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> for
      the full scope of that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who can use it</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is intended for painting contractors and small painting
      businesses acting in a professional or business capacity. You must
      be able to form a legally binding contract to purchase Pro.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      There are no user accounts, usernames, or passwords on the Site.
      Free tools require nothing to use. Pro access is unlocked by a
      license key tied to your Dodo Payments purchase — see "Purchases and
      license keys" below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Purchases and license keys</h2>
    <p>
      Pro is a one-time purchase ({PRICE.amount}, lifetime access — no
      subscription) processed by our payment provider, Dodo Payments. When
      your payment succeeds, we generate a license key from that payment
      and email it to you. That key is what unlocks Pro in your browser —
      keep it somewhere safe, since we have no account system to look it
      up other than by re-verifying it against your original payment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prices are shown in the currency displayed at checkout and may
      change for future purchases; a change in price never affects a
      purchase you've already made.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      You can request a full refund of your Pro purchase within{" "}
      <strong>7 days</strong> of the original payment date — just{" "}
      <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with the email you paid with. If we
      approve a refund and Dodo Payments processes it, your Pro license is
      deactivated automatically the next time it's checked; your local
      project data is never deleted as part of a refund. Requests made
      after the 7-day window are considered at our discretion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your data, your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      All estimate and project data you create lives in your own browser's
      local storage — we never receive or store a copy of it (see the{" "}
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>). This means:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We can't recover your data if you clear your browser, switch
        devices, or lose access to the device you used.
      </li>
      <li>
        Backing up your own data (via the tool's export feature) is your
        responsibility.
      </li>
      <li>
        A refund, license issue, or account dispute has no effect on your
        locally-stored data either way — we have no ability to touch it
        remotely, for better or worse.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Attempt to circumvent, reverse-engineer, or defeat the license/
        payment verification system.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the contact form or any part of the Site to send spam, abuse,
        or unlawful content.
      </li>
      <li>
        Interfere with the Site's normal operation (e.g. attempting to
        overload or attack it).
      </li>
      <li>Resell, sublicense, or redistribute a Pro license key.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Site's design, code, calculators, and branding belong to us. Your
      own estimate/project data, and anything you type into the tools,
      belongs to you — we don't claim any ownership of it, and (as covered
      above) we don't even have a copy of it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No warranty; limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is provided "as is," without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including accuracy, fitness for a particular
      purpose, or uninterrupted availability. See the{" "}
      <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> for the specific limits on the
      calculations themselves.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total liability to you
      for any claim relating to the Site is limited to the amount you
      actually paid us in the 12 months before the claim (i.e. up to
      {PRICE.amount} for a Pro purchase, or $0 if you only used the free
      tools). We aren't liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential
      damages, including lost profits or lost business, arising from your
      use of the Site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using the Site at any time. We may suspend or revoke
      Pro access if your payment is refunded or reversed, or if we
      reasonably believe you've violated the acceptable-use section above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change, we'll update the date at the top of this
      page. Continued use of the Site after a change means you accept the
      updated terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
